; The `@duplicates reject` policy on array-shaped set collections (phase 1 of the per-rule
; duplicates policy). `reject` swaps the transparent alias target from `Vec`/`NonEmptyVec` to the
; uniqueness twin `OrderedSet`/`NonEmptyOrderedSet`, whose single `TryFrom` door refuses a duplicate
; (a `DeserializeFailure::DuplicateKey(Key::Uint(index))`) on both the wire and the API. Accepted
; (duplicate-free) input still re-emits byte-exactly — the twin is order-preserving, never sorted —
; so `reject` only NARROWS the accepted set, it never touches the accepted bytes.
;
; - `int_set`   — `[*]` tagged-or-untagged set idiom, reject flavor -> `OrderedSet<u64>`.
; - `int_neset` — `[+]` flavor, reject -> `NonEmptyOrderedSet<u64>` (its door composes uniqueness
;                 with the `[+]` min-1 `RangeCheck`, one type, not a nested wrapper).
; - `text_set`  — untagged arm FIRST + a text element: arm order and element kind are irrelevant to
;                 both the collapse and the policy.
; - `oset_u64`  — a NAMED generic instance of a reject-flavored generic def, proving the policy
;                 survives generic use-site re-resolution (the collapse stores the already-collapsed
;                 reject body; the instance resolves to a transparent `OrderedSet<u64>` alias).
; - `plain`     — a plain (non-idiom, untagged, no tag-258) array rule carrying reject: pre-Conway
;                 Cardano sets are untagged arrays, and the alias-target swap is the identical seam.
; - `holder`    — embeds the reject rules in record-field position (incl. an OPTIONAL field) so the
;                 member-side (de)serialize and optional-field wrapping compile and round-trip.
int_set = #6.258([* uint]) / [* uint] ; @duplicates reject
int_neset = #6.258([+ uint]) / [+ uint] ; @duplicates reject
text_set = [* text] / #6.258([* text]) ; @duplicates reject
oset<a0> = #6.258([* a0]) / [* a0] ; @duplicates reject
oset_u64 = oset<uint>
plain = [* uint] ; @duplicates reject
holder = [s: int_set, ns: int_neset, g: oset_u64, p: plain, ? t: text_set]
